# The codes that left the catalog (docs/decisions/015-errors-are-a-closed-set-writes-answer-an-outcome.md,
# "A code leaves by a recorded withdrawal"). One row a code:
#   set | code | shipped in | left in | why
# A row is for a sentence the product can no longer say, never for a rename, and it stays:
# `scripts/refusals.py` refuses a shipped code that is gone without its row, and a code of a
# row that is in the catalog, so a withdrawn code is not used again.
